    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7">

                <pb facs="0018" n="6" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">741.45C/10–1746: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Rangoon</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Packer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-10-18T18:00:00-05:00">October 18, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>242. Following received from London.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“8903 Oct 17. Exchange Burma commissioners discussed informally today with
                        Burma office which professed be without knowledge governor’s plans this
                        connection. Official indicated when question arises in future Burma office
                        thinking probably would parallel that in Dept’s reply quoted Deptel
                        7084 Oct 9. He thought it possible Burma might want announce appointment
                        commissioners UK, India and US simultaneously.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
